      "translation": {
        "english_text": "(with a faint smile) Plot! Uma!... The word 'sathi' has a frightening meaning when it stands alone. Join 'pati' to sathi and make 'sathipathi'... and it takes on a sacred meaning!",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The source makes a Tamil wordplay between `சதி` (plot/conspiracy, and in the compound invoked here a wife-related form) and `பதி` (husband/lord). The English retains the source terms rather than manufacturing an unrelated pun."
        ]
      }
